  "animations": {
    "idle": {
      "duration": 2,
      "loop": true,
      "note": "One breath, one 5 deg nod inside it, and a ripple that never stops travelling down the ears. The nod is the same projection `bow` holds at 12: dy = y (cos t - 1) - z sin t about a horizontal axis through the skull, so the head plate keys a `pitch` transform and the features key a `pitch` derive with a depth each. The ripple is a `wave` whose PHASE is the only thing that moves - 45 deg per key, nine keys, so 360 deg lands exactly on the duration and the cycle closes on its own opening geometry. The ripple keys carry no easing on purpose: a travelling wave moves at constant speed, and an eased cross-fade between two sinusoids stutters twice per period. The two ears differ in amplitude and start a quarter-period apart, which is what stops them reading as one animation played twice.",

      "tracks": [
        {
          "bone": "torso",
          "property": "scale",
          "keys": [
            { "t": 0, "v": [1, 1], "ease": "swell" },
            { "t": 0.95, "v": [1.006, 1.012], "ease": "swell" },
            { "t": 2, "v": [1, 1] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "bone": "chest",
          "property": "translatey",
