    "bow": {
      "duration": 1.8,
      "loop": false,
      "note": "A 12 deg nod, anticipated, held and released - the angle README.md's fold-angle table is about. Every number in it is one line of arithmetic on dy = y (cos t - 1) - z sin t, so the spec states that line and the depths it reads and the compiler states the numbers (AUTHORING 4.11.1 and 4.5.1). The anticipation is the part worth reading: it is the SAME model at -4 deg, one key on each of the four tracks, and FACE 1.1 says outright that a hand-transcribed table priced this out. `facebob` carries the shift every feature shares (-R sin t); the `features` group carries each feature's own depth below the skull surface times sin t, which is why the snout - the only part in FRONT of the surface - is the only negative residual. The ears hang off `head` rather than off `facebob`, so they take no derive at all: their swing is a judgement per member and it is spelled as a `v` map, which is the other half of AUTHORING 4.5.1 and the right half for a mirrored pair. The ripple's amplitude rides the swing and its phase keeps advancing, landing on 360 deg past where it started so `bow` ends on the geometry `idle` opens with.",

